cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "qiskit-zksf: Qiskit provider for the Zero Kelvin Simulation Foundry"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21851381
message: "If you use this provider or the certification protocols it surfaces in published work, please cite the protocol paper as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ZKSF.org (Zero Kelvin Simulation Foundry)"
    email: info@zksf.org
    website: "https://zksf.org"
  - name: "Digital Venture Labs LLC"
repository-code: "https://github.com/official-dvl/qiskit-zksf"
url: "https://zksf.org"
abstract: >-
  Qiskit provider exposing ZKSF simulation engines and quantum hardware as
  BackendV2 backends, so existing Qiskit circuits run against exact statevector,
  tensor-network, stabilizer, Pauli-propagation, noisy or real-hardware engines
  by changing the backend rather than the code. Every approximate result carries
  a documented accuracy statement under the ZCC-v0.1 protocol, or a measured
  hardware fidelity under ZHF-v0.1, reachable through job.error_info(). Each
  engine is a separate backend with its own qubit limit and gate set, so a
  circuit an engine cannot run is rejected at transpile time rather than after
  submission.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - qiskit
  - qiskit provider
  - quantum circuit simulation
  - tensor networks
  - error bounds
  - certification
license: MIT
